<title>ITALY: FAO sees increased feed use of cereals in 1996/97.</title>
<headline>FAO sees increased feed use of cereals in 1996/97.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Nations Food and Agriculture Organisation (FAO) said on Monday that global animal feed use of cereals was forecast to expand by 2.3 percent in 1996/97 after a sharp downturn in the previous year.</p>
<p>Its latest food outlook said feed use of cereals, representing about one third of total world utilisation, was seen expanding by 14.5 million tonnes to 643 million.</p>
<p>&quot;The forecast increase in feed use would be about half of the estimated drop in 1995/96,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>FAO said most of the partial recovery in feed use was expected to be in the developed world.</p>
<p>&quot;Wheat and coarse grains used for feed are likely to rise by 5.2 percent and 1.9 percent respectively,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>((-- Rome newsroom 39 6 678 2501))</p>
</text>
